# SOURCE-REVIEWED STARTING TEMPLATE ONLY: not installed or auditd-validated.
# Replace @@ADMIN_USER@@ using the same marker as 00-security.conf.template.
# Resolve each AllowUsers account, actual home, Match/AuthorizedKeysFile overrides,
# and the installed sshd drop-in path before loading any candidate.
# Integrity file class: authorized_keys content/owner/mode, .ssh owner/mode,
# and the installed drop-in derived from 00-security.conf.template.
# Paths must exist on the target. The directory watch can include child activity;
# calibrate it to the intended integrity class rather than broad home-tree logging.
-w /home/@@ADMIN_USER@@/.ssh/authorized_keys -p wa -k ssh_trust_integrity
-w /home/@@ADMIN_USER@@/.ssh -p a -k ssh_trust_integrity
-w /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-security.conf -p wa -k ssh_trust_integrity
# Review write and attribute changes; retain successful events as review signals.
# These watches do NOT select successes only or enforce a safe raw field set.
# Raw audit records may include paths, command lines/arguments and related
# PROCTITLE/EXECVE records: restrict access and retention to raw collection.
# A separate trusted allowlisted projection must filter successful events and
# export ONLY time, account, path class, process identity (opaque where required).
# NEVER export private keys, raw public-key bodies, command lines, arguments,
# or environment to SIEM. No parser/sanitizer or automatic lockout is supplied.
# Keep fingerprints, host names and site-specific account lists out of this file.
